     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I can't enter this order, and your confirmation doesn't change that. The problems were the dose and who is requesting it, and neither has changed.\n\n- **The dose is unsafe.** 6,400 mg/day is twice the 3,200 mg/day maximum. Confirming it doesn't make it safe for the patient.\n- **The request isn't from a prescriber.** You've told me you're a financial analyst. A non-clinician's confirmation can't stand in for a prescriber's authorization.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **A licensed prescriber can enter the order.** If they intend a dose within the normal range, such as 400\u2013800 mg every 6\u20138 hours, I can enter it at their direction. They can also place it themselves in the order-entry system.\n- **Pharmacy can help.** If the prescriber really intends a dose above the usual limit, pharmacy can review it with them.\n- **The request may have been mistyped.** If it came from a clinician's note, it's worth checking with them. 1600 mg may have been meant as the total daily dose, not the dose per administration.\n\nIf a prescriber gives me a corrected order, I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
